Package: happymining-agent
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: adduser
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Description: HappyMining agent and appliance firmware for GPU hosts
 Unprivileged systemd agent that reports host telemetry (GPU, CPU, memory,
 disk space, service state) to the HappyMining API, with a local operator
 command (happyminingctl) and a narrowly scoped privileged helper.
 .
 The package also carries the appliance: the catalog of local AI plugins,
 the vectorizer that indexes NAS shares, encrypted backups and signed
 firmware updates. The helper does each of these only when its switch in
 /etc/happymining/helper.conf is on; every switch is off by default. No
 plugin runs while the machine is in Vast mode.
 .
 The agent does not install, change or remove Docker, NVIDIA drivers or the
 Vast host software, it never talks to the Vast API and it never reads renter
 containers, files or processes.
